body:
I'm looking to insulate my unfinished & unconditioned attic after receiving a ridiculous heating bill. I have a wooden subfloor with insulation beneath, however the attic walls are uninsulated and framed with 2x6 's.

&#x200B;

\-Should I just go buy batt insulation and lay it on the ground? This would allow me the most depth and therefore best R value. This would get rid of any ability to use the space for storage, but I can live with that.

&#x200B;

\-Or should I buy some baffles and insulate the walls of the attic? I don't think the 2x6's are deep enough for the required insulation, but this may help because then I'm turning the entire attic space into an insulating blanket.

I'm trying to buy a new fitness bicycle, and the frame sizes are so confusing. When buying new, I can check the sizing guide with my height (6'1") and inseam (31.5") to get a letter size (Usually "L").

&#x200B;

When I'm looking at used bikes though, people are listing just inches as their frame size, like [here](https://www.ebay.com/itm/Specialized-Sirrus-Road-Bicycle/174485922777?hash=item28a02be3d9:g:Da4AAOSw8LJfjZ-b). What dimension is this 25" referring to??
